<article class="env-remark" id="9BBA18">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/9BBA18">Remark <span data-tag="9BBA18">6.3.5.7</span>.</a> Corollary <a href="/tag/B83FF1" data-tag="B83FF1">6.3.5.6</a> implies in particular the existence of homotopy fiber sequences </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calZ }( 1_{\calZ }, \phi ^{\ast } U ) \rightarrow \bHom _{ \LGeom }( \calX _{/U}, \calZ ) \rightarrow \bHom _{\LGeom }(\calX , \calZ ) \]
</div>
  <p> (where the fiber is taken over a geometric morphism $\phi ^{\ast } \in \bHom _{\LGeom }(\calX , \calZ )$). </p>
  <p>Suppose that $\calZ = \calX _{/V}$, and that $\phi ^{\ast }$ is a right adjoint to the projection $\calX _{/V} \rightarrow \calZ $. We then deduce the existence of a canonical homotopy equivalence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calX }(V,U) \simeq \bHom _{\calZ }( 1_{\calZ }, \phi ^{\ast } U ) \simeq \bHom _{ \LGeom _{\calX /}}( \calX _{/U}, \calX _{/V} ). \]
</div>
</article>